\subsection{F1: All Variable-Rate Configurations Degrade}
\label{sec:f1}

Every configuration that introduces $\dt > 1$ imagination degrades relative to the $\dt{=}1$ baseline, regardless of mechanism (Figure~\ref{fig:learning_curves}). The baseline (exp\_001) reaches 915.7 at 105K steps and peaks at 970.4 at 505K. In contrast, fixed $\dt{=}2$ (exp\_006) peaks at 485.3 at 35K before collapsing to 132.9 by 65K---a $-73\%$ decline from its own peak (14\% of baseline). Fixed $\dt{=}4$ (exp\_007) peaks at only 176.9 at 25K and never exceeds 152.5 thereafter. The learned-gate configuration (exp\_005) peaks at 541.2 at 55K but collapses to 98.8 by 145K. This uniform degradation motivates the factorial analysis that follows.

